    <string name="setup_1_title">What this does</string>
    <string name="setup_1_body">This add-on puts a button on your movies and episodes in SeriesGuide. Tap it, and the exact title opens in Stremio, in Fireguy, or in either one. You pick next.</string>
    <string name="setup_choice_title">Which apps do you use?</string>
    <string name="setup_choice_body">The button only opens the apps you pick. You can change this any time in Settings.</string>
    <string name="setup_2_title">Turn it on in SeriesGuide</string>
    <string name="setup_2_body">The button only appears after you switch the extension on inside SeriesGuide. Open Extensions and enable “Open in Stremio”.</string>
    <string name="setup_3_title">Make sure it’s installed</string>
    <string name="setup_3_body_stremio">The button opens Stremio, so grab it if it isn’t on your device yet. It’s free.</string>
    <string name="setup_3_body_fireguy">The button opens Fireguy On Demand. Fireguy isn’t on Google Play, so install it the way you were given it.</string>
    <string name="setup_3_body_both">Install Stremio from Google Play (it’s free) and Fireguy the way you were given it. With both installed, the button asks which one you want.</string>
    <string name="setup_4_title">You’re all set</string>
    <string name="setup_4_body">That’s it. Open any movie or episode in SeriesGuide and look for the “%1$s” button.</string>
    <string name="setup_open_sg_extensions">Open SeriesGuide → Extensions</string>
